.TH GET_COW_STATS 2 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
sys_pmap_stats \- get pmap and virtual memory statistics
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/arch/i386/pmap.h>
.LP
.BI "int sys_pmap_stats(struct pmap_stats *" out ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sys_pmap_stats
retrieves global virtual memory statistics from the kernel.
.PP
The
.I out
argument points to a
.B pmap_stats
structure:
.PP
.RS
.nf
struct pmap_stats {
    uint32_t faults;                /* Total page faults */
    uint32_t cow_faults;            /* COW faults */
    uint32_t zero_fills;            /* Zero-fill faults */
    uint32_t protection_upgrades;   /* Read->Write upgrades */
    uint32_t protection_downgrades; /* Write->Read downgrades */
    uint32_t cow_pages_mapped;      /* Pages shared via COW */
    uint32_t cow_duplications;      /* Pages duplicated by COW */
    uint32_t pages_saved_by_cow;    /* Pages saved by COW optimization */
    uint32_t tlb_invlpg_count;      /* TLB single page flushes */
    uint32_t tlb_full_flush_count;  /* TLB full flushes */
    uint32_t total_pmaps;           /* Current allocated pmaps */
};
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned. On error, -1 is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.I stats
points to an invalid address.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmap (9)
